k for 20.1 uh members  separately um but first of all let's do  members of the cabinet and i do have  apologies this evening  from both councillor whitehead and  councillor alban  so councillor duckworth can you confirm  you're here  here thank you and councillor yates  i'm here thank you now before i come to  uh item 20.1 i have to announce i'm  afraid that item four  has been withdrawn or i am withdrawing  it  and the reason for that is that uh it's  been pointed out to me this morning  quite helpfully  by a member of the public um that the uh  one of the documents  circulated with item four is not uh  the appropriate document to go with the  pool version of that document  and i think in the issue in the interest  of transparency  we ought to be circulating the correct  document with the report so that  everybody can consider it  um and we can have a proper discussion  on that basis i wasn't keen that we  circulated the correct version tonight  when the public haven't had an  opportunity to see it  so my intention is that we'll bring that  item back to the august meeting and i do  apologize to  members and to members of the public who  may have joined the stream in order to  see what we had to say about that item  but we won't be considering it tonight  so i did have a number of members who  wanted to speak on item for but  obviously there's nothing to speak about  does anybody wish to speak on any other  item this evening  doesn't appear so okay  so i've already dealt with apologies um  does anybody ever declare any  declarations of interest for any item of  business on the agenda this evening  no time to take that as read minutes of  the previous meeting to approve the  summary and recommendations and  decisions of the cabinet meeting held on  the 18th of june  copy of which is attached to the agenda  pack um i will propose the minutes to  have a seconder  i'll second that that's the duck with  second in it  uh unless i hear any objection i'll take  those as app